      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-33957",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve $r(t) = e^{t}(\\sin ti + \\cos tj + \\sqrt{2}k)$, $t \\ge 0$, for which the arc length from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s = 2(e^{t} - 1)$. Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s$, what is the $y$-component of $R$?"
